Package: patrone-shell-config
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: command-not-found, zsh, zsh-syntax-highlighting, zsh-autosuggestions
Description: shell setup for PatroneOS users
 Gives bash, the default shell, Patrone's two-line prompt (blue for normal
 users, red for root), through a ~/.bash_aliases that new users get from
 /etc/skel, and root gets when the package is installed. For users who
 choose zsh, it also installs a .zshrc and .zprofile with the same prompt,
 syntax highlighting and suggestions from history.
 .
 Common Windows commands typed in a shell, from CMD and PowerShell, such as
 ipconfig or Get-ChildItem, are refused with the Linux command to use
 instead. It only prints: a program of that name always runs first, and any
 other unknown command gets Ubuntu's usual suggestion of a package.
 .
 Windows and PowerShell are trademarks of the Microsoft group of companies.
